@flexiarg baldwin/plasticity-builds-a-selective-neighbourhood
@title Plasticity Must Expose Inherited Differences to Selection
@sigils [🎑/门]
@keywords fitness-landscape, learning, selection, hinton-nowlan, neighbourhood, gradient
@audience evolutionary-computation researchers, fitness designers
@tone causal
@style pattern
@childof baldwin/mechanism
@references [baldwin/assimilation-requires-a-resolved-path]
@references-extra ["Hinton and Nowlan (1987), https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~hinton/absps/evolution.htm" "Paenke, Kawecki and Sendhoff (2009), The influence of learning on evolution"]

! conclusion:
  Lifetime plasticity guides evolution only if post-learning fitness varies
  systematically with inherited proximity to, or bias toward, useful phenotypes.
  Plasticity must create a selective neighbourhood, not merely rescue every genotype
  to the same score.

  + context:
    In Hinton and Nowlan, a correct fixed allele removes a guess, an incorrect fixed
    allele prevents success, and `?` leaves a binary trial to learning. Genotypes with
    more correct fixed decisions therefore succeed more often or sooner. The learning
    process converts an isolated target into graded heritable evidence.

  + IF:
    Learning can reach high function from multiple inherited starting points.

  + HOWEVER:
    If learning erases the effect of initial genotype, all successful learners are
    selectively equivalent. If fitness records only final band membership, faster or
    cheaper learners may also be indistinguishable. Plasticity then shields genetic
    variation rather than guiding it.

  + THEN:
    Measure fitness as a vector containing raw function, probability of reaching the
    target, time or rewrites to target, and generalization across tasks. Before a paid
    run, verify that controlled inherited perturbations induce correctly ordered
    post-learning fitness differences.

  + BECAUSE:
    Evolution cannot read the learned state directly. It can only retain inherited
    causes correlated with reproductive success. Learning supplies guidance by making
    that correlation smoother or denser than the unlearned landscape.

    + COUNTERFACTUAL:
      If two inherited fields produce the same post-learning fitness distribution
      despite different learning work, no selection operator can infer which one is
      closer to the useful developmental trajectory.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Add a preregistered inherited-perturbation response curve to MetaCA preflight.
    - Replace the band-only scalar with lexicographic or Pareto-preserving function and effort measurements.
